WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.830
Researchers studied members
of gyms in the United States.

2
00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:08.040
Members on monthly contracts
paid over 70 dollars a month.

3
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.730
On average, they went 4.3 times a month.

4
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.110
That works out at more
than 17 dollars a visit.

5
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.760
Yet a 10-visit pass cost
just 10 dollars a visit.

6
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.990
So why would anyone sign up for the dearer

7
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.210
deal and then hardly go?

8
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.820
In this mission, you'll
meet the biases that pull

9
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.750
real choices away from the rational model,

10
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.170
from rules of thumb to anchoring.

11
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.130
Then you'll judge whether economists
should give up on the idea of rational

12
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.390
choice. Your mission: explain
why so many people pay

13
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.400
for a gym they hardly use.
